      "id": "chu-6-3-2",
      "locus": "Chāndogya Upaniṣad Bhāṣya 6.3.2",
      "cite": "sankara/chandogya-upanisad-bhasya/6.3.2-sadatmana",
      "source_label": "ChU Bh 6.3.2",
      "iast": "sarvaṃ ca nāmarūpādi sadātmanaiva satyaṃ vikārajātaṃ svastvanṛtameva",
      "english": "All name-and-form and the like is true only with Sat as its Self; the class of modifications is untrue in its own right.",
      "grammar": "sarvaṃ is the subject. ca links the series. nāmarūpādi is a collective nominal expression, 'name-and-form and the like'. sadātmanaiva is sat-ātmanā eva in sandhi: 'with Sat alone as its Self'. satyaṃ and anṛtam are the opposed predicates. vikārajātaṃ is the arisen class of modifications. svastvanṛtameva is svatas tu anṛtam eva in sandhi, an adverbial exclusion: 'however, in its own right, untrue'.",
