      "iast": "kāraṇāt paramārthato ’nanyatvaṃ vyatirekeṇābhāvaḥ kāryasya",
      "english": "Ultimate non-otherness from the cause is the effect’s absence when the cause is excluded.",
      "grammar": "kāraṇāt is apādāna, ablative of separation: 'from the cause'. paramārthataḥ is an adverbial ablative, 'ultimately / in ultimate truth'. ’nanyatvam is the abstract noun 'non-otherness'. vyatirekeṇa is an instrumental of exclusion: 'by exclusion, apart from'. abhāvaḥ is the nominal predicate 'absence'. kāryasya is a genitive dependent on abhāvaḥ: 'of the effect'.",
