      "source_label": "Anuvyākhyāna 1.4.111–12",
      "iast": "jīveśvarabhidā caiva jaḍeśvarabhidā tathā /\njīvabhedo mithaścaiva jaḍajīvabhidā tathā /\nmithaśca jaḍabhedo yaḥ prapañco bhedapañcakaḥ //\nso 'yaṃ satyo hyanādiśca sādiścennāśamāpnuyāt /\ndvaitaṃ na vidyata iti tasmādajñānināṃ matam //",
      "english": "The world is the fivefold difference: difference of jīva and Lord, of insentient matter and Lord, of jīvas from one another, of matter and jīva, and of insentient things from one another. This is real and beginningless; if it had a beginning, it would come to destruction. Therefore the statement “duality does not exist” is the view of the ignorant.",
