      "iast": "śuddhaḥ sākṣī yadā siddho duḥkhitvaṃ vāryate katham /\nupajīvyapramāṇaṃ tad bhedagrāhakam eva hi /\nato jīveśayor bhedaḥ śrutisāmarthyasusthiraḥ //\ntathāpi tu cidānandapūrvāstatsadṛśā guṇāḥ /\nsārasvarūpamasyāpi muktāvapyavaśiṣyate //\nato 'bhedavadevaitāḥ śrutayaḥ pravadanti hi /\npaurāṇāni ca vākyāni sādṛśyābhedasaṃśrayāt //\nsādṛśyācca pradhānatvāt svātantryādapicābhidām /\nāhurīśena jīvasya na svarūpābhidāṃ kvacit //",
      "english": "When the pure witness is established, how can the condition of being a sufferer be denied? That means of knowledge on which one relies apprehends difference. Therefore the difference between jīva and Lord is firmly established by the force of scripture. Yet qualities beginning with consciousness and bliss still remain as similar to that [Lord], and the essential nature of this [jīva] remains even in liberation. Therefore these scriptural statements speak as if of non-difference. The Purāṇic statements do so too, because they rest on similarity-grounded non-difference. And because of similarity, primacy, and sovereignty, they apply Lord-language to the jīva, but never essential identity.",
